    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Solve the following quadratic equation by using the quadratic formula:

\[ {@a*v^2+b*v+c@} = 0. \] 
<br>
Give your answer as a set \(\left(e.g. \left\{x_1 , x_2\right\} \right)\): <br>
<br>
\({@v@} \in \) [[input:ans]] [[validation:ans]] [[feedback:prt1]]]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>To solve for \[ {@a*v^2+b*v+c@} = 0. \]  using quadratic formula, we substitute the values of a, b and c into the formula below.</p>


<p>\[ x = \frac {-b \pm \sqrt{b^2-4ac} }{2a}. \]</p>

<p> Since \(a = {@a@}\), \(b = {@b@}\), \(c = {@c@}\), then:</p>

\[ {@v@} = \frac{{@(-b)@} \pm \sqrt{{@b^2@}-({@4*a*c@})}}{@2*a@} = {@-b/(2*a)@} \pm {@(sqrt(b^2-4*a*c))/(2*a)@}. \]

Therefore \( {@v@} = {@ta1@}\) or \( {@v@} = {@ta2@}\) and so the solution set is: 

\[ {@v@} \in {@{ta1  , ta2}@}. \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
